## Context
Author ruling, 2026-10-27 raid (1249's doifetch half, options B then C). DOIfetch is a separate project
(`MinhHaDuong/DOIfetch` on GitHub, a fork of `hanhan6688/DoiHarvest`), not a script to vendor. Colleagues
asked for it, so it must install in one command. Step B lands in the DOIfetch repo: a console entry point
`doifetch`, open and institutional sources (Crossref, Unpaywall, HAL, ISTEX, EZproxy) as the default
source list, and a README install line (`uv tool install git+https://github.com/MinhHaDuong/DOIfetch`).
The harness neither adds nor enables shadow-library sources; enabling any source outside the default
list stays a manual, per-user choice.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `idh install` installs DOIfetch as a uv tool pinned to a recorded ref (or reports clearly that uv or
      the network is unavailable), idempotently; a test on a temporary HOME with a stubbed `uv`.
- [ ] The zotero skill gains a "fetch missing fulltexts" step that calls `doifetch` with the default
      (open and institutional) source list only, for the works the cited-works check reports missing, and
      says what to do when `doifetch` is absent.
- [ ] Tracker 1249's doifetch child line points here; the harness gate passes.

## Relevant files
adapters/lifecycle.py, bin/idh, skills/zotero/SKILL.md, skills/zotero/references/*, tests/test_idh_lifecycle.py

